# saturday
## The second shift
$ do discover("the_coin_by_the_yards")
The second shift begins at eleven. You can hear it from a mile. When the whistles go, a great wave of men in aprons goes in through the Exchange Avenue gate with the lamps at their backs and the pens before them, and the whole of the smell of the Yards rises into the cold air in a single column, as of a very large animal breathing out.
?if coven_size() > 0 and b6.circle == "all"
  {_reader_name} has said, in the front hall, quite flatly, that the family will not let you go alone. It is not a request.
  :the_company
  * Go alone, and let them wait in the cars at the gate
    $ b6.company = "alone"
    $ cunning_brutal += 1
    They do not like it. They say so, with the exactness of people who have said it before. They are, at the end, as they have always been, your arm. They will be at the gate.
  * Bring the family, and let the Yards see what it is dealing with
    $ b6.company = "family"
    $ standing += 2
    $ secrecy -= 1
    They go in with you, a little behind, in a long dark line, as a family goes to a christening. The men at the gate step back. It is not a thing that they decide.
?else
  $ b6.company = "alone"
  There is no one at your shoulder. It is a long walk down the Exchange Avenue road with the lamps going out behind you.
?end
